<h2 id="stories" class="section-title">Short Stories</h2>

<div class="card">
<h3>The Selfish Giant</h3>
<ul>
<li>A giant has a beautiful garden.</li>
<li>Children play there every day.</li>
<li>The giant drives the children away.</li>
<li>He builds a wall around the garden.</li>
<li>Spring never comes because of selfishness.</li>
<li>The garden stays in winter.</li>
<li>Children secretly enter the garden.</li>
<li>The giant realizes his mistake.</li>
<li>He becomes kind.</li>
<li>The garden becomes beautiful again.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>The Oval Portrait</h3>
<ul>
<li>A traveler stays in an old castle.</li>
<li>He sees many paintings.</li>
<li>One portrait attracts him.</li>
<li>The painting shows a beautiful woman.</li>
<li>The painter was her husband.</li>
<li>He loved art deeply.</li>
<li>He kept painting her.</li>
<li>The woman became weak.</li>
<li>The painting became perfect.</li>
<li>The woman died.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>God Sees the Truth but Waits</h3>
<ul>
<li>Aksionov is a merchant.</li>
<li>He is wrongly accused of murder.</li>
<li>He is sent to prison.</li>
<li>He spends many years there.</li>
<li>He becomes religious.</li>
<li>The real murderer arrives.</li>
<li>Aksionov learns the truth.</li>
<li>He forgives the criminal.</li>
<li>The criminal confesses.</li>
<li>Aksionov dies peacefully.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>The Wish</h3>
<ul>
<li>A boy plays alone.</li>
<li>He imagines the carpet as danger.</li>
<li>Black lines mean death.</li>
<li>He walks carefully.</li>
<li>His imagination grows.</li>
<li>He feels fear.</li>
<li>The game becomes serious.</li>
<li>He tries not to touch lines.</li>
<li>Fear increases.</li>
<li>The story shows imagination.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Civil Peace</h3>
<ul>
<li>The story occurs after a war.</li>
<li>Jonathan survives with family.</li>
<li>He repairs his bicycle.</li>
<li>He earns money.</li>
<li>He starts a business.</li>
<li>The government pays him.</li>
<li>Thieves steal his money.</li>
<li>He stays calm.</li>
<li>He remains hopeful.</li>
<li>Life is more important than money.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Two Little Soldiers</h3>
<ul>
<li>Two soldiers are friends.</li>
<li>They visit countryside Sundays.</li>
<li>They enjoy nature.</li>
<li>One meets a milkmaid.</li>
<li>He falls in love.</li>
<li>He visits her alone.</li>
<li>Friend becomes lonely.</li>
<li>Friendship weakens.</li>
<li>The lonely soldier becomes sad.</li>
<li>He jumps into the river.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>An Astrologer's Day</h3>
<ul>
<li>An astrologer works in a market.</li>
<li>He pretends to predict futures.</li>
<li>He actually guesses.</li>
<li>A stranger visits him.</li>
<li>The astrologer becomes nervous.</li>
<li>The man was his old enemy.</li>
<li>The astrologer lies.</li>
<li>He says attacker is dead.</li>
<li>The man believes him.</li>
<li>The astrologer feels relieved.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2 id="poems" class="section-title">Poems</h2>

<div class="card">
<h3>Corona Says</h3>
<ul>
<li>The coronavirus speaks to humans.</li>
<li>It warns about harming nature.</li>
<li>Humans destroy forests.</li>
<li>Animals suffer.</li>
<li>Nature reacts.</li>
<li>Humans must change.</li>
<li>Respect nature.</li>
<li>Stop greed.</li>
<li>Live in balance.</li>
<li>Protect the environment.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>A Red Red Rose</h3>
<ul>
<li>The poet expresses love.</li>
<li>Love is like a red rose.</li>
<li>It is fresh and beautiful.</li>
<li>Love is like sweet music.</li>
<li>The poet promises forever love.</li>
<li>Distance cannot change it.</li>
<li>He will return.</li>
<li>Time cannot destroy love.</li>
<li>The poem celebrates romance.</li>
<li>Love is eternal.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>All the World's a Stage</h3>
<ul>
<li>The world is compared to a stage.</li>
<li>People are actors.</li>
<li>Life has seven stages.</li>
<li>Infant stage.</li>
<li>Schoolboy stage.</li>
<li>Lover stage.</li>
<li>Soldier stage.</li>
<li>Justice stage.</li>
<li>Old age stage.</li>
<li>Life ends.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Who Are You Little I</h3>
<ul>
<li>A child watches the sunset.</li>
<li>The sky is beautiful.</li>
<li>The child feels amazed.</li>
<li>The world feels magical.</li>
<li>The child feels small.</li>
<li>The universe is big.</li>
<li>Nature is wonderful.</li>
<li>The moment feels special.</li>
<li>Curiosity grows.</li>
<li>The poem shows innocence.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>The Gift in Wartime</h3>
<ul>
<li>The poem describes war.</li>
<li>A soldier dies.</li>
<li>His body is destroyed.</li>
<li>His body parts are sent home.</li>
<li>His wife receives them.</li>
<li>She feels deep sadness.</li>
<li>War destroys families.</li>
<li>People suffer loss.</li>
<li>War is cruel.</li>
<li>Peace is important.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2 id="essays" class="section-title">Essays</h2>

<div class="card">
<h3>Sharing Tradition</h3>
<ul>
<li>Traditions connect people.</li>
<li>They show identity.</li>
<li>They link ancestors.</li>
<li>Culture includes art and stories.</li>
<li>Elders must teach youth.</li>
<li>Culture must be preserved.</li>
<li>Traditions strengthen communities.</li>
<li>Sharing keeps culture alive.</li>
<li>Respect traditions.</li>
<li>Protect cultural heritage.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>How to Live Before You Die</h3>
<ul>
<li>Based on Steve Jobs speech.</li>
<li>Life lessons from experience.</li>
<li>Failure teaches success.</li>
<li>Follow your passion.</li>
<li>Life is short.</li>
<li>Do not fear mistakes.</li>
<li>Work hard.</li>
<li>Trust yourself.</li>
<li>Listen to your heart.</li>
<li>Live fully.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>What I Require from Life</h3>
<ul>
<li>Life should be adventurous.</li>
<li>Knowledge is important.</li>
<li>Learning never stops.</li>
<li>Creativity matters.</li>
<li>Challenges are good.</li>
<li>Boring life is not fulfilling.</li>
<li>Curiosity grows knowledge.</li>
<li>Explore ideas.</li>
<li>Use imagination.</li>
<li>Life should be exciting.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>What Is Poverty</h3>
<ul>
<li>Poverty means hunger.</li>
<li>Poor people suffer daily.</li>
<li>They lack food.</li>
<li>Clothes are poor.</li>
<li>Homes are uncomfortable.</li>
<li>Poverty brings shame.</li>
<li>Children suffer most.</li>
<li>Society ignores them.</li>
<li>Poverty harms mind and body.</li>
<li>The essay shows harsh reality.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Scientific Research Is a Token of Humankind's Survival</h3>
<ul>
<li>Science helps humanity.</li>
<li>Research solves problems.</li>
<li>Technology improves life.</li>
<li>Medicine saves lives.</li>
<li>Scientists study nature.</li>
<li>New discoveries help progress.</li>
<li>Research prevents disasters.</li>
<li>Knowledge is power.</li>
<li>Countries must support science.</li>
<li>Human survival depends on research.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2 id="plays" class="section-title">One Act Plays</h2>

<div class="card">
<h3>Trifles</h3>
<ul>
<li>John Wright is murdered.</li>
<li>Police investigate.</li>
<li>Two women observe clues.</li>
<li>Men ignore details.</li>
<li>Women notice a dead bird.</li>
<li>The bird belonged to Mrs Wright.</li>
<li>Her husband killed it.</li>
<li>She killed him.</li>
<li>Years of suffering caused it.</li>
<li>Women hide the evidence.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>A Sunny Morning</h3>
<ul>
<li>The play occurs in Madrid.</li>
<li>Two old people meet.</li>
<li>They argue at first.</li>
<li>They recognize each other.</li>
<li>They were lovers.</li>
<li>Love ended long ago.</li>
<li>They are now lonely.</li>
<li>They remember their past.</li>
<li>They imagine a happy story.</li>
<li>The play shows nostalgia.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Refund</h3>
<ul>
<li>Wasserkopf returns to school.</li>
<li>He wants his money back.</li>
<li>Teachers test him again.</li>
<li>He answers poorly.</li>
<li>Teachers help him secretly.</li>
<li>They avoid refund.</li>
<li>He passes exam.</li>
<li>No refund is given.</li>
<li>The situation is humorous.</li>
<li>The play criticizes education.</li>
</ul>
</div>

</div>

